{
  "coverage": "BooleanLists (family 2) with surface operands (shim kinds 2 plane and 3 sphere). solidcore copies each surface with the virtual Copy (WR-196), so a list of surfaces makes one face per surface over its natural domain, and two lists of planes take the planar 2D path; upstream's base copy constructor slices every surface to a geometry-less SmSurface, so there any list that has surfaces and no B-rep ends the call with SM_ERR (1001). The cases cover each list position, both kinds, a shell vertex and a box as the other operand, an empty other list, an invalid operation, options and extreme scales. A list that has B-reps ignores its surfaces (upstream reads the surface list only when the B-rep list is empty), so the three mixed cases compare real results. expected_status is solidcore's.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "plane_list_vs_plane_list",
      "inputs": {
        "family": 2,
        "operation": 1,
        "options": null,
        "a": [
          {
            "point": [
              0,
              0,
              0
            ],
            "surface": {
              "plane": {
                "normal": [
                  0,
                  0,
                  1
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "b": [
          {
            "point": [
              0,
              0,
              0
            ],
            "surface": {
              "plane": {
                "normal": [
                  0,
                  1,
                  0
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        ],
        "tree": []
      },
      "expected_status": 1007,
      "note": "Two planes that are not coincident take the planar 2D path, which refuses them (invalid input)."
    },
